-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_jobs._atomic_write_json","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_write","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore.create"],"claim":"A durable job keeps its id, receipt path and original request immutable; repeated identical requests reuse their receipt and conflicting requests are rejected.","id":"proofs-b.harness.identity","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore.finish","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore.mark_started","grant_agent.harness_jobs._atomic_write_json","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_write","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore.start","grant_agent.harness_job_worker.run_harness_job"],"claim":"Completion and interruption remain terminal; blockers preserve actionable evidence until explicit cancellation; cancellation claims and stopped jobs cannot be revived by late worker events. Actual detached start is single-flight under concurrent callers; actual early-cancelled workers return before backend import; positively dead cancelling workers finalize cancelled.","id":"proofs-b.harness.lifecycle","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_job_worker._arm_runtime_budget","grant_agent.harness_job_worker._claim_runtime_budget_exhaustion","grant_agent.harness_jobs._atomic_write_json","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_write","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore.cancel","grant_agent.harness_jobs._terminate_process_tree","grant_agent.harness_job_worker._start_runtime_budget_watchdog","grant_agent.harness_job_worker._record_runtime_budget_enforcement_failure","grant_agent.harness_job_worker._record_runtime_budget_enforced"],"claim":"Arming deducts durable startup delay; cancellation and settlement preserve other budget dimensions; exhausted budgets retain their original exhaustion receipt and cancelled jobs release still-active budgets. Verified owned process-tree termination stops descendants; operator cancellation releases active budgets and real deadline cancellation retains exhaustion. Actual owned-child termination denial preserves an armed active budget after failed operator cancellation; real deadline enforcement records retry attempts while denial remains, then stops the child after access restoration before its safety exit. Retry history and unrelated budget dimensions remain durable.","id":"proofs-b.harness.budget","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore._sync_admission_policy_locked","grant_agent.harness_execution_capacity.HarnessExecutionCapacity._sync_policy_locked","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_write"],"claim":"Admission and execution policy limits are integers within retention, may tighten across instances, cannot expand ambiently, and unreadable policies fail closed.","id":"proofs-b.harness.policy","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_jobs._with_job_observability","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_observation"],"claim":"Observed timings and ordered timeline phases derive from durable timestamps; receipts remain unchanged; blocked runs remain nonterminal and every list row has additive metrics.","id":"proofs-b.harness.observation","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore.create","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore._capacity_snapshot","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_admission","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore._reconcile_admission_receipts","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore._prune"],"claim":"Serialized admission counts every unresolved, blocked, unknown or unreadable receipt; terminal outcomes release capacity; concurrent creates cannot exceed the durable operator limit. Admission scans beyond the visible hundred-row list; unsupported future terminal schemas survive pruning and consume capacity.","id":"proofs-b.harness.admission","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_execution_capacity.HarnessExecutionCapacity.try_acquire","grant_agent.harness_job_worker._mark_waiting_for_execution_capacity","grant_agent.harness_job_worker._claim_execution_capacity","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_execution_snapshot"],"claim":"Only the oldest waiting job acquires bounded OS slots; legacy and unreadable active receipts reserve capacity, held and crash-released locks remain authoritative, waiting workers stay running to prohibit duplicate launch.","id":"proofs-b.harness.execution","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_jobs._exclusive_job_lock","grant_agent.harness_jobs._job_guard_path","grant_agent.harness_jobs.HarnessJobStore.load","grant_agent.harness_jobs._process_alive","grant_agent.harness_jobs._windows_process_alive","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_liveness_outcome"],"claim":"Mutation uses bounded stable OS guard shards; live old legacy owners and recent malformed compatibility fences remain fail closed, even with a short caller-specific wait; aged tokenized locks serialize until actual guard release, and dead owners recover. Non-destructive Win32 liveness uses observed synchronization waits or ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER=87 as positive death; indeterminate errors retain ownership. Actual owned-child Win32 ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED=5 and unavailable command-line lookup retain live ownership and admission pressure; only that child DACL is temporarily changed, restored through the retained creation handle, and the child is reaped.","id":"proofs-b.harness.lock-recovery","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_job_worker._hard_runtime_budget_seconds","grant_agent.harness_job_worker._remaining_runtime_budget_seconds","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_budget_input"],"claim":"Explicit hard runtime budget priority is nested, canonical, then snake-case; booleans, invalid, negative and platform-unsupported timeouts fail closed, malformed persisted startup timestamps expire immediately.","id":"proofs-b.harness.budget-input","impact":["durable local harness actions","operator capacity and saved evidence"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_registry.save_harness_profile","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_profile"],"claim":"Saved profiles contain only public route fields and credential environment-variable names; unknown raw secret fields never persist.","id":"proofs-b.harness.public-profile","impact":["harness public configuration","explicit route and credential boundaries"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_registry.harness_gateway_environment","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_gateway"],"claim":"Gateway overlays preserve exact explicit harness/profile/model/base routing and map runtime credential references into the correct auth surfaces; Claude CLIProxy requires explicit loopback HTTP and a present credential, while Rook derives the exact provider from its key name.","id":"proofs-b.harness.gateway","impact":["harness public configuration","explicit route and credential boundaries"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_registry._validate_instruction_path","grant_agent.harness_registry.save_harness_instruction","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_instruction"],"claim":"Instruction edits stay within supported workspace files, preserve prior bytes in a recoverable backup and return byte-accurate saved receipts; path escape is rejected.","id":"proofs-b.harness.instruction","impact":["harness public configuration","explicit route and credential boundaries"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.harness_registry.build_harness_catalog","grant_agent.harness_registry._probe_harness_command","grant_agent.runtimes.base.runtime_bin_candidates","grant_agent.proofs_b_harness.check_catalog"],"claim":"The canonical current catalog includes all sixteen harnesses including Hermes/OpenClaw with truthful security, transport, public gateway and extension ownership; missing supplied provider configuration remains setup-required, native release probing uses intrinsic evidence and existing home uv-bin discovery remains available.","id":"proofs-b.harness.catalog","impact":["harness public configuration","explicit route and credential boundaries"],"phase":"invariant"}
-- @proof {"checkedAt":["grant_agent.runtimes.managed_cli.normalize_managed_cli_model"],"claim":"Valid Grok custom models remain exact; a foreign Claude model requires explicit allow_custom policy and otherwise fails closed.","id":"proofs-b.harness.model-policy","impact":["harness public configuration","explicit route and credential boundaries"],"phase":"invariant"}
